To make the circle element appear more 3D in CSS, you can add some depth and shadows using the following CSS properties:

1. Perspective: This property adds a 3D effect by creating a virtual viewing point. Set this value for the parent container (#chart-area) to give the circles a sense of depth.

   ```css
   #chart-area {
     perspective: 800px;
   }
   ```

2. Transform: Use translateZ() to move the circle forward or backward in the z-axis, giving it a sense of depth. You can also use rotateX(), rotateY(), and rotateZ() to tilt the circle.

   ```css
   .circle {
     transform: translateZ(100px); /* move circle forward */
     transform: rotateX(-30deg); /* tilt the circle */
     transform: rotateY(-15deg); /* tilt the circle */
   }
   ```

3. Box-shadow: Add a box-shadow with a blur radius to create a shadow beneath the circle.

   ```css
   .circle {
     box-shadow: 0px 5px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
   }
   ```

4. Background: Use a linear gradient for the background color to add depth and texture to the circle.

   ```css
   .circle {
     background: radial-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5)), conic-gradient(#f5c0cb 0deg, transparent 0deg, transparent 90deg);
     background-size: contain;
   }
   ```

